From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dcomp: DCompositionCreateDevice2/3, device 2 interfaces, GetIids, async action, SetRenderingDevice (3615)

dcomp: DCompositionCreateDevice2/3, device 2 interfaces, GetIids, async action, SetRenderingDevice

DCompositionCreateDevice2 and 3 now make a device that answers
IDCompositionDevice2 and IDCompositionDesktopDevice (the same object as the
original device, with the desktop methods forwarding to it); IDCompositionDevice3's
extra effects are not offered. IDCompositionDesktopDevice::CreateSurfaceFactory
returns a factory that makes surfaces on the rendering device given. GetIids
of every WinRT composition object lists its runtime interfaces, the activation
factory names its class, ICompositorController::EnsurePreviousCommitCompletedAsync
returns an already completed IAsyncAction/IAsyncInfo, and
ICompositionGraphicsDeviceInterop::SetRenderingDevice replaces the device and
context (drawing surfaces start empty on the new device at their next
BeginDraw). CreateSurfaceFromHandle/Hwnd stay unimplemented (ESCALATE.md).

Browser-facing: Firefox asks for DCompositionCreateDevice2/3; run the dcomp
and browser checks at integration.
